.SS hidpp_error_code
.PP
.nf
\fBHIDPP_API int hidpp_error_code(hidpp_receiver_t *rcv);\fR
.fi
.PP
Returns the HID++ error code (\fBenum hidpp_protocol_error\fR) the device
answered the last request of \fBrcv\fR with, or 0 if the last request did not
fail that way. Requests answered by an error report fail with HIDPP_EIO,
so this is what tells them apart from transport failures and from each
other (for example "busy" from "invalid argument").
.SS hidpp_protocol_error_str
.PP
.nf
\fBHIDPP_API const char *hidpp_protocol_error_str(int code);\fR
.fi
.PP
Returns a human\-readable string for a HID++ error code.
