.SS hidpp_input_type
.PP
.nf
\fBHIDPP_API int hidpp_input_type(hidpp_input_t *input, const char *text);\fR
.fi
.PP
Types out \fBtext\fR as a sequence of key presses/releases, applying
shift automatically for uppercase letters and shifted punctuation.
Only covers the printable US\-layout ASCII range plus '\et' and '\en';
unmappable characters are skipped. Returns HIDPP_OK, or a negative
hidpp_error if \fBfd\fR is invalid.
.SS hidpp_input_move
.PP
.nf
\fBHIDPP_API int hidpp_input_move(hidpp_input_t *input, int dx, int dy);\fR
.fi
.PP
Simulates a relative mouse movement of (\fBdx\fR, \fBdy\fR) pixels/counts.
.SS hidpp_input_button
.PP
.nf
\fBHIDPP_API int hidpp_input_button(hidpp_input_t *input, int button, int value);\fR
.fi
.PP
Simulates a press (\fBvalue\fR != 0) or release (\fBvalue\fR == 0) of a
mouse button (see enum hidpp_mouse_button).
.SS hidpp_input_scroll
.PP
.nf
\fBHIDPP_API int hidpp_input_scroll(hidpp_input_t *input, int dx, int dy);\fR
.fi
.PP
Simulates scroll wheel movement. \fBdy\fR is vertical scroll (positive is
up), \fBdx\fR is horizontal scroll (positive is right); either may be 0.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
For functions that return signed integers, a 0 indicates that the function exited successfully.
If instead a negative number is returned, it indicates a specific error that occurred during function's execution.
The returned error codes are made to resemble POSIX in both meaning and numeric value.
.PP
The lifetime of most objects is tied to the parent \fIhidpp_receiver_t\fR object.
The exception to this are input handlers from \fIhidpp_input_open\fR.
